# Binary fixtures must survive checkout byte for byte.
#
# Without this, git's line-ending conversion rewrites LF to CRLF on Windows,
# which corrupts any file whose format counts bytes. A PDF stores byte offsets
# in its xref table, so a converted checkout produces a file that is structurally
# invalid — and the failure appears as "this PDF has no pages" on one platform
# only, which points nowhere near the cause.
*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.gguf  binary
*.wasm  binary
